  status: smoke
description: 'v031''s exact recipe with ONE change: input_proj 64 -> 96, so the 224-wide
  transformed row is compressed 2.3x instead of 3.5x. Recurrent trunk untouched at
  hidden 128.'
hypothesis: "THIS IS NOT A CAPACITY EXPERIMENT, and that is the whole point. Every\
  \ recurrence-widening result says extra parameters get absorbed as overfitting.\
  \ But the input projection is a different animal: at 64 units it is a 3.5x BOTTLENECK\
  \ on the 224-wide level-plus-difference row, and a bottleneck destroys information\
  \ rather than merely adding variance.\n\n  dozken's audit put a number on it --\
  \ \"the 224->64 projection destroying ~0.014 WP of linearly available signal\" --\
  \ and then measured it at -0.0032 on his chunk4k recipe. That does not settle it\
  \ for us, because chunk4k is a recipe his own data shows is HARMFUL under Global\
  \ WP (-0.0370 vs reset4k), making it the wrong substrate to measure a projection\
  \ change on. We have never varied input_proj on OUR recipe.\n\n  It is also nearly\
  \ free where the trunk was not: the projection is 6.4% of per-row compute, so widening\
  \ it 1.5x costs about 3% latency, against the 2x-4x that blew the budget for v026\
  \ and v027.\n\n  Prediction: if the bottleneck hypothesis is right this GAINS where\
  \ added recurrence lost, because it feeds the recurrence more signal without giving\
  \ it more parameters to overfit with. Flat or negative joins head_hidden and hidden\
  \ on the closed-capacity list."
change_vs_parent: model.input_proj 64 -> 96 only. Recurrent trunk, distill_weight,
  schedule and seed all unchanged.
